      "writtenOn": "2020-01-28T10:07:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is to redirect names like \"libfoo.vendor.29.arm64\" to \"libfoo\" or \"libfoo.vendor\". The reason why the arch suffix is from ctx.DeviceConfig() is that the suffix represents the primary arch of target devices. For example, \"libfoo.vendor.29.arm64\" might have both arm and arm64 .so files, and they will be used for arm64 devices. Whileas \"libbar.vendor.29.arm\" will only have one arm64 .so file.\n\nBut thinking again, this logic seems very fragile and unstable. I changed this logic to directly use dep module.",
      "parentUuid": "6b0bbb23_acbc0907",
